I dive two days at Shelly Beach in a row and get blessed with some incredible visibility. This place is seriously an awesome shore dive site, to walk straight from your car into the water is INSANE. Some awesome things seen were goatfish changing colour with their chromatophores and silver trevally swimming over the top of each other for food.

## Dive stats

- **Location:** Shelly Beach, NSW
- **Date:** 8 June 2026
- **Depth:** Max Depth 12.2m, Avg Depth 6.5m
- **Visibility:** 10-15m

## Highlights

Spotted wobbegong, giant cuttlefish, old wife, silver trevally, eastern red scorpionfish.
